    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Explain locked bodies in Request and Response clone()]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/46567</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/46567"/>
        <updated>2026-11-17T14:57:06.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36569722?u=919b278a71956b9b30fea93a71dd49a50e81b168&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">Both clone() pages only mention a body that has already been used. Acquiring a body reader also makes cloning throw TypeError, even before the first read and while bodyUsed remains false.</p>
<p dir="auto">Document the locked-body case and explain the getReader() trigger on both Request and Response. This follows Fetch's clone algorithms and its definition of an unusable body:<br>
<a href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-request-clone" rel="nofollow">https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-request-clone</a><br>
<a href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-response-clone" rel="nofollow">https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-response-clone</a></p>
<p dir="auto">Checked in Node 24.22.0 for both interfaces: an unread locked body throws, releasing the unread reader lock allows cloning, and a consumed body still throws. Targeted Prettier and git diff --check pass. No browser or full content build run.</p>]]></content>
        <author>
